------------------------------------- Custom pipe with date-fns -----------------------------------------

- BUILD OUR OWN PIPE USING THE THIRD PARTY LIBRARY date-fns TO DISPLAY PRETTY DATES.

- Instruction: Angular Prerequisite "Pipes" chapter

1️⃣ Install date-fns: npm install date-fns


2️⃣ Generate a custom pipe named PrettyDate inside the folder shared/pipes or wherever you want:

        ng g p shared/pipes/pretty-date


3️⃣ Implement the pipe:
    Earlier in the chapter 13: Pipes/section 10. creating our own pipe, we saw how to create our
    custom pipe.

        transform(value: string, ..._args: Array<unknown>): string {
            const date = parseISO(value);
            return formatDistanceToNowStrict(date, { addSuffix: true });
        }
       
    
    ⚠️ But there are some drawback to this:
    ❌ transform(value: string) only accepts strings but doesn't handle the Date object, null/undefined.
        Angular templates frequently receive undefined values during initialization. So the better code
        would be:
        
        transform(value: string | Date | null | undefined): string {
            if (!value) {
                return '';
            }
            const date = typeof value === 'string' ? parseISO(value) : value;
            return formatDistanceToNowStrict(date, {
                addSuffix: true
            });
        }


4️⃣ Import and use the pipe:  <p>{{ raceModel().startInstant | prettyDate }}</p>


